WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.024
- McDonald-duh.

00:00:01.024 --> 00:00:01.857
- McDonald.

00:00:01.857 --> 00:00:02.690
- McDonald-duh.

00:00:02.690 --> 00:00:03.690
- Duh.
- Duh.

00:00:05.233 --> 00:00:07.816
(upbeat music)

00:00:14.198 --> 00:00:15.031
Hi, I'm Evan,

00:00:15.031 --> 00:00:17.057
and I'm here in my
mother land South Korea,

00:00:17.057 --> 00:00:17.890
Seoul,

00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:19.289
with a few of my American friends,

00:00:19.289 --> 00:00:21.250
and we are about to try
some Korean McDonald's.

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:23.169
A.k.a. McDonald-duh.

00:00:23.169 --> 00:00:24.002
The items on the menu here,

00:00:24.002 --> 00:00:25.389
I heard it's really crazy.

00:00:25.389 --> 00:00:27.196
It's a lot different
than the ones in America,

00:00:27.196 --> 00:00:29.279
let's see if you like it.

00:00:31.046 --> 00:00:32.733
- So we are having Korean McDonald's.

00:00:32.733 --> 00:00:33.566
Me for the first time,

00:00:33.566 --> 00:00:34.764
you for the first time in what?

00:00:34.764 --> 00:00:36.037
- Fifteen years, I think.

00:00:36.037 --> 00:00:37.268
I'm not a huge fast food guy so,

00:00:37.268 --> 00:00:39.141
even though I visit Korea,

00:00:39.141 --> 00:00:41.501
I actually never visit McDonald's.

00:00:41.501 --> 00:00:43.677
This is as new to me as it is to you.

00:00:43.677 --> 00:00:45.062
- I haven't had that much McDonald's.

00:00:45.062 --> 00:00:47.092
I probably had it when I
was a kid a couple of times.

00:00:47.092 --> 00:00:49.660
I'm willing to try it
because we're in Korea.

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:51.198
- I think I'm going to
enjoy Korean McDonald's

00:00:51.198 --> 00:00:52.893
because I'm all about those options.

00:00:52.893 --> 00:00:53.726
I've been dying to try it.

00:00:53.726 --> 00:00:55.059
- Let's do this.

00:00:56.632 --> 00:00:57.465
- Double,

00:00:57.465 --> 00:00:58.298
Bulgogi,

00:00:58.298 --> 00:00:59.160
burger.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:00.163
- [Andrew] Wow, this is saucy.

00:01:00.163 --> 00:01:01.891
- Kinda looks like sausage.

00:01:01.891 --> 00:01:03.315
- You know when you picture Bulgogi,

00:01:03.315 --> 00:01:05.531
it's like sliced, shredded meat.

00:01:05.531 --> 00:01:08.371
I was expecting to see like
Arby's roast beef burger.

00:01:08.371 --> 00:01:09.691
- It does smell like Bulgogi though.

00:01:09.691 --> 00:01:11.363
- It's a double sausage patty burger

00:01:11.363 --> 00:01:14.770
with some Bulgogi marinade on it.

00:01:14.770 --> 00:01:15.603
- It's pretty good.

00:01:15.603 --> 00:01:16.928
- Yeah. I don't hate it.

00:01:16.928 --> 00:01:18.958
- Not bad, but not Bulgogi.

00:01:18.958 --> 00:01:20.399
- It is really saucy though.

00:01:20.399 --> 00:01:24.233
A little bit too saucy for me, saucy boy.

00:01:24.233 --> 00:01:25.066
(speak foreign language)

00:01:25.066 --> 00:01:28.123
(men laughing loudly)

00:01:28.123 --> 00:01:29.995
- The Supreme Shrimp burger.

00:01:29.995 --> 00:01:33.027
Koreans are really into
their shrimp-y snacks.

00:01:33.027 --> 00:01:34.563
Then their squid-y snacks.

00:01:34.563 --> 00:01:35.638
- I got to tell you something, Steven.

00:01:35.638 --> 00:01:38.005
- What?
- I'm allergic to shrimp.

00:01:38.005 --> 00:01:41.387
- [Steven] Fine, give it to me.

00:01:41.387 --> 00:01:43.067
- It is so shrimp-y inside.

00:01:43.067 --> 00:01:44.771
- Wait, there's actual shrimp in there.

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:46.355
- It's actually a shrimp.

00:01:46.355 --> 00:01:47.875
I was expecting a paste.

00:01:47.875 --> 00:01:49.596
- This is the fish-o-filet of Korea.

00:01:49.596 --> 00:01:52.163
- It's got that popcorn shrimp taste,

00:01:52.163 --> 00:01:54.899
that battered, fried shrimp appeal.

00:01:54.899 --> 00:01:55.732
Shrimp-y.

00:01:56.971 --> 00:01:59.139
- McSpicy Shanghai chicken burger.

00:01:59.139 --> 00:02:01.883
- Got a big ol' chicken thing happening.

00:02:01.883 --> 00:02:03.603
- This is probably the
only fast food burger

00:02:03.603 --> 00:02:05.739
that the patty is actually
bigger than the bun.

00:02:05.739 --> 00:02:08.579
(loud chewing)

00:02:08.579 --> 00:02:09.412
- Okay.

00:02:11.091 --> 00:02:12.283
- It's a little bit spicy,

00:02:12.283 --> 00:02:15.717
but all of the spice is coming
from inside the chicken.

00:02:15.717 --> 00:02:16.878
- You can taste the chicken

00:02:16.878 --> 00:02:18.693
a lot better than you can
taste the chicken in America.

00:02:18.693 --> 00:02:20.478
- The chicken is not mushy at all.

00:02:20.478 --> 00:02:22.022
The texture of the meat is there.

00:02:22.022 --> 00:02:24.334
- It's general chewy spiciness.

00:02:24.334 --> 00:02:26.046
- It's not like pepper spicy.

00:02:26.046 --> 00:02:28.182
You're not getting the different flavor

00:02:28.182 --> 00:02:30.349
you would get from a jalapeno
or something like that.

00:02:30.349 --> 00:02:32.951
- I got that spice coming in
on the back when I chewed in.

00:02:32.951 --> 00:02:36.240
It's like flirting with my mouth.

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:37.073
- Churro.

00:02:37.073 --> 00:02:38.082
Does that say churro?

00:02:38.082 --> 00:02:39.848
(speaks foreign language)

00:02:39.848 --> 00:02:44.650
- There's a serious amount of
the cinnamon sugar on here.

00:02:44.650 --> 00:02:46.260
- You know, it's definitely not a churro,

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:48.924
but I would buy it just because it's good.

00:02:48.924 --> 00:02:50.620
- There's three different sauce options.

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:54.029
- Strawberry, which is
apparently radioactive.

00:02:54.029 --> 00:02:56.612
- [Adam] It's like alien blood.

00:02:58.349 --> 00:02:59.221
- Very sweet.

00:02:59.221 --> 00:03:01.653
- If you just melted down
some strawberry lollipops,

00:03:01.653 --> 00:03:03.421
that's what this dip is like.

00:03:03.421 --> 00:03:05.671
- Caramel. Oh that's thick.

00:03:07.121 --> 00:03:08.786
- It's probably the way
to go with this one.

00:03:08.786 --> 00:03:10.273
- I would just eat it plain, to be honest.

00:03:10.273 --> 00:03:11.593
- Yeah. It's already sweet.

00:03:11.593 --> 00:03:14.089
- So bread-y. It's so dense.

00:03:14.089 --> 00:03:15.105
I do enjoy it.

00:03:15.105 --> 00:03:16.273
- How do you say chocolate in Korean?

00:03:16.273 --> 00:03:19.515
(speaks foreign language)

00:03:19.515 --> 00:03:21.346
- It's distinctly Hershey's syrup.

00:03:21.346 --> 00:03:24.306
- Exactly what I was gonna say.

00:03:24.306 --> 00:03:26.545
- Okay. Overall, I do enjoy McDonald's.

00:03:26.545 --> 00:03:28.801
McDonald's in Asia is more
upscale, more luxurious.

00:03:28.801 --> 00:03:30.210
I enjoyed the foods that were here.

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:31.891
- The spicy chicken burger,

00:03:31.891 --> 00:03:32.905
I think that was really great.

00:03:32.905 --> 00:03:35.116
If these burgers were
presented in America...

00:03:35.116 --> 00:03:35.949
- [Steven] Oh yeah.

00:03:35.949 --> 00:03:37.822
- I feel crazy right now.

00:03:37.822 --> 00:03:40.405
(upbeat music)

00:03:43.789 --> 00:03:45.299
(squeaking)

